        "finding": "Consolidated summary at step 9 (for the specific architecture '1D_CNN'):\n**Memory Consolidation Entry**\n\n**Strategic Learnings**\n\n*Hyperparameter Optimization*\n- Optimal learning rate range: ~0.0001-0.00013\n- Moderate dropout rates (~0.12-0.14) outperform higher rates (>0.27)\n- Deeper convolutional architectures (6-8 layers) significantly enhance performance\n- Larger filter sizes (128 vs 64) contribute to better model outcomes\n\n*Performance Indicators*\n- Learning speed strongly predicts final accuracy (0.91 correlation)\n- Standard deviation of accuracy serves as reliable overfitting indicator (0.73 correlation)\n- Lower learning rates correlate with both higher accuracy (-0.80) and lower validation loss (-0.92)\n- Best performers converge faster (22.5 vs 33.2 epochs) with superior stability\n\n*Architecture Insights*\n- Standard 1D_CNN (0.9303 accuracy) outperformed residual CNN (0.8960 ceiling)\n- Progressive improvements achievable through targeted parameter adjustments\n- Training dynamics outweigh architectural complexity in impact\n\n**Corrective Lesson**\n\n*Successful Strategies*\n1. **Evidence-Based Parameter Selection**: Leveraged correlation analysis to identify key drivers - learning rate (77.3% importance), kernel size, and learning speed\n2. **Systematic Complexity Reduction**: Effectively decreased convolutional layers (12\u219210) and dropout rates (0.27\u21920.14) based on negative performance correlations\n3. **Comparative Architecture Validation**: Early benchmarking revealed performance ceilings, enabling timely pivots from limited architectures\n4. **Progressive Optimization Approach**: Demonstrated consistent accuracy improvements (0.4778\u21920.8357\u21920.8960) through targeted adjustments\n\n*Critical Learning Points*\n- **Training Dynamics Priority**: Focus on learning rate scheduling and epoch management before architectural complexity when correlations indicate stronger relationships with optimization parameters\n- **Early Validation Protocol**: Compare against simpler baselines early to avoid resource investment in fundamentally limited architectures\n- **Convergence Monitoring**: Track discrepancy between set and actual training epochs as early indicator of training instability\n- **Strategic Pivoting**: When architectures consistently underperform despite optimization, transition to proven alternatives rather than pursuing diminishing returns\n- **Resource-Efficient Testing**: Use correlation analysis to guide parameter selection, but verify hypotheses with focused trials before broad sweeps\n\n*Implementation Guidelines*\n- Address convergence instability with learning rate scheduling before extending training duration\n- Maintain std_accuracy monitoring as early warning system for overfitting\n- Balance architectural depth (6-8 convolutional layers) with training parameter optimization\n- Prioritize computational resources toward parameters with strongest correlation evidence",
